  "goodToKnow": "Die Pfarrei is a parish, especially a Catholic one; Protestants usually say die Kirchengemeinde. Der Pfarrer (die Pfarrerin) is the parish priest or pastor, and das Pfarrhaus the vicarage. With church membership in Germany falling below half the population in 2022 and few new priests, many Pfarreien are being merged into large units. Church members pay church tax (Kirchensteuer). Plural: die Pfarreien."
